# Local values for `wrangler dev`. Copy to .dev.vars, which Git ignores, and
# uncomment only the values you set: a value here overrides wrangler.toml
# [vars], and an empty value overrides it with an empty string.
#
# Deployed environments do not define these in wrangler.toml; set them with:
#   npx wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <environment>

# Tally API key for the governance routes
# TALLY_API_KEY=

# node-provider-proxy used for every JSON-RPC call, as
# https://<NODE_PROXY_HOST>/<network>/<NODE_PROXY_KEY>; the host has no scheme
# and the key may be empty. `npm start` reads the chain through the deployed
# proxy these name; with wrangler.local-proxy.toml, which binds the proxy run
# on this machine instead, leave them unset (README.md, Getting Started)
# NODE_PROXY_HOST=
# NODE_PROXY_KEY=

# Public host of this API
# V3_API_HOST=

# Optional Blocknative API key for /legacy/mainnet/gas-price
# BLOCK_NATIVE_API_KEY=

# Comet registry admin API: the SHA-256 of the admin bearer token, as 64 hex
# digits, never the token itself
# COMET_REGISTRY_ADMIN_TOKEN_HASH=

# Optional name the registry records as the actor of every administrative
# change: activations and rollbacks, overlay events, and the syncs it asks
# for. Unset, it is registry-admin:<ENVIRONMENT>
# COMET_REGISTRY_ADMIN_ACTOR=

# GitHub token the registry import reads the Comet repository with: optional
# here, required in stage and production. Without one GitHub allows 60 API
# requests an hour per address, which a Worker shares with every other Worker
# leaving Cloudflare through it. A fine-grained token with read-only access
# to public repositories, and no other permission, is enough
# COMET_GITHUB_TOKEN=
